What is Conductive Silver Paste?
Conductive silver paste is a specialized electronic material composed of silver particles (flakes or nanoparticles) suspended in polymer/resin binders with solvents and additives. This versatile formulation offers superior electrical conductivity, thermal properties, and adhesion strength, making it indispensable for various electronic applications. The material serves as the conductive element in solar cell electrodes, printed circuit boards, RFID antennas, and multiple sensor technologies.

